# Project: synesthesia-experiments

## Context
This is a research-art project exploring synesthetic visualization 
of sound on the web. The author is a Japanese freelance web developer 
aiming for MIT Media Lab.

## Tech stack
- p5.js (loaded via CDN, not npm)
- Web Audio API (Amplitude, FFT)
- Plain HTML/JS, no framework
- Vite for local dev only

## Code style
- Keep code short and readable
- Prefer explicit names over clever abbreviations  
- Comment the WHY, not the WHAT
- Use HSB color mode for all color work

## Design philosophy
- Browser-native: must work without installation
- The hand of the author should remain visible
- AI helps with implementation, not aesthetic decisions
- Reference: Marks (1975) on cross-modal correspondence

## Constraints  
- No localStorage/sessionStorage (Vite local dev fine, but be aware)
- Test on phone (Vercel preview) before merging to main
- Each major change = new branch + commit

## Current version
v0.1.4 - three-axis mapping (hue/saturation/brightness)

## Known issues
- Centroid calculation skews high for noise (clap reads "blue")
- Voice frequencies cluster in 1-2 FFT bins
- AirPods ANC pre-processes the signal (use raw mic when possible)